<https://w3id.org/eudpp/> a owl:Ontology;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/eudpp/ACTOR>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/COMP>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/CON>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/EVENT>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/IDENT>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/MAT>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/P_DPP>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/SOC>;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "\n        [1] Robal, T., Maigre, R., Haav, H.M., 2026. Ontology requirements for digital product passports based on the ecodesign for sustainable products regulation. Procedia Computer Science 277, 356–365. DOI:10.1016/j.procs.2026.02.077. <br/><br/>\n\n        [2] Maigre, R., Robal, T., Haav, H.M., 2026. Modular ontology design approach for an ESPR compliant digital product passport core ontology,in: Joint Proceedings of Baltic DB&IS Conference Forum and Doctoral Consortium 2026 co-located with 17th International Baltic Conference on Digital Business and Intelligent Systems (Baltic DB&IS 2026), CEUR-WS.org, Tartu, Estonia. pp. 115–126. URL: https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-4211/paper11.pdf. <br/><br/>\n\n        [3] Maigre, R., Haav, H.-M., Robal, T., Wolf, M.-A., Danash, F. (2025). Ontology Requirements Specification for an EU DPP Core Ontology Proposal (Version 1.1). CIRPASS-2 Consortium. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15270342. <br/><br/>\n        "@en;
    dcterms:contributor "Daniel Hutzschenreuter"@en, "Elio Hbeich"@en, "Fatima Danash"@en, "Gisa Foyer"@en, "Hele-Mai Haav"@en, "Jens Niederhausen"@en, "Marc-Andree Wolf"@en, "Theodor Chirvasuta"@en;
    dcterms:created "2025-02-27"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:creator "Riina Maigre"@en, "Tarmo Robal"@en;
    dcterms:description "\n        The CORE is the integration ontology that imports all the specific ontology modules and the connector (bridge) ontology of these.\n        ---\n        Note on the license: This ontology is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). In case of dispute over CC BY 4.0 applicability, or in case considering the ontology as a software or part of it, this ontology is to be considered licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.\n        ---\n        THIS DOCUMENT IS PROVIDED WITH NO WARRANTIES WHATSOEVER. \n        All liability for any damages arising from use or misuse of this vocabulary is with the user.\n        "@en;
    dcterms:issued "2026-10-30"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    dcterms:title "CORE  of the EU DPP core ontology proposed by the CIRPASS-2 project."@en;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "eudpp";
    rdfs:comment "The CORE of the EU DPP core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    rdfs:label "EU DPP CORE"@en;
    owl:versionInfo "2.2.0".
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/ACTOR> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:contributor "Hele-Mai Haav"@en, "Tarmo Robal"@en;
    dcterms:created "2025-03-14"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:creator "Riina Maigre"@en;
    dcterms:description "Actor module of an EU DPP core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project.\n\nDEPENDENCIES:  This module has dependencies to the following EU DPP Core Ontology modules: CON, P_DPP, EVENT.  \n\nFor more information, see \nMaigre, R., Haav, H.-M., Robal, T., Wolf, M.-A., &amp; Danash, F. (2025). Ontology Requirements Specification for an EU DPP Core Ontology Proposal (1.1). CIRPASS-2 Consortium. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15270342\n---\nNote on the license: This ontology is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). In case of dispute over CC BY 4.0 applicability, or in case considering the ontology as a software or part of it, this ontology is to be considered licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.\n---\n"@en;
    dcterms:issued "2026-10-30"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    dcterms:title "Actors and roles module for an EU DPP core ontology proposed by CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "act";
    rdfs:comment "The Actor module of an EU DPP core ontology proposed by the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    rdfs:label "EU DPP CO ACTOR"@en;
    owl:versionInfo "2.3.0".
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/COMP> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15270342>;
    dcterms:contributor "Gisa Foyer"@en, "Jens Niederhausen"@en;
    dcterms:created "2026-06-05";
    dcterms:creator "Daniel Hutzschenreuter"@en;
    dcterms:description "The ESPR refers to the EU Declaration of Conformity (EU-DoC) as a key element to provide knowledge on compliance with regulatory requirements for relevant products. Thus, the design of the ontology module for compliance was focused on establishing information and relations between information to provide the EU-DoC in a reliable form and according to the requirements set out in Article 44 and Annex V of the ESPR. For developing the ontology model, the following competency questions guided the basic design of the underlying knowledge graph.  \n\n Q1: Provide all information from the DPP relevant to be presented with the EU-DoC (extract the EU-DoC). \n\nQ2: Did the manufacturer declare an authorized representative to issue the EU-DoC? \n\nQ3: Which Union Harmonised Legislation is applied for the product? \n\nQ4: Which product requirements need to be fulfilled for the product? \n\nQ5: Which notified bodies did an assessment of the product requirements according to which conformity assessment modules?\n---------\nThe compliance module introduces the class EUDeclarationOfConformity as knowledge graph node to access all information required by the ESPR Annex V for the EU-DoC. Objects from the Product and Actor ontology modules provide substantial information in the context of the EU-DoC and relevant links are provided through the Connector ontology. In particular, EUDeclarationofConformity is a subclass of the Document product property. Different Actor objects can be linked to identify the entities such as the issuer of the EU-DoC, its signer, the product manufacturer or the authorized representative on behalf of the manufacturer. It is important to note, that an Actor who is the manufacturer must provide the Actor role assignment to the manufacturer's role. If an authorized representative is provided, the Actor must provide an Authorized representative assignment linked to the manufacturer's role. \n\nIn addition, the compliance ontology provides classes for defining the Union Harmonisation Legislation, Product Requirements such as harmonized standards, common specifications or other technical specifications, Conformity Assessment Modules and Certificates.\n\nThe EU-DoC class refers to the relevant Union Harmonisation Legislation, and each legislation refers to the applicable product requirements used for presumption of conformity. An additional object property is provided to directly link the product with the Union Harmonisation Legislation it is in conformance with. Finally, the Union Harmonisation Legislation class has a data property allowing to link the European Legislation IDs (ELI) from the European Common Data Model (http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/cdm). \n\nNotified bodies, who assess conformity of the product with the Union Harmonisation Legislation, are represented using the Actor ontology too. The linked Actor object  must provide the Actor role assignment to the role of a notified body. The data property of this Actor object must provide the NANDO numbering system as operator identifier scheme and the NANDO number of the underlying notified body as operator ID. All notified bodies within Europe are listed with a unique number in the NANDO repository (https://webgate.ec.europa.eu/single-market-compliance-space/notified-bodies).  \n\nNotified bodies assess compliance with requirements from Union Harmonisation Legislation according to predefined conformity assessment modules as defined by the New Legislative Framework the ESPR is aligned to (http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec/2008/768(1)/oj). The notified bodies are linked through object properties to the applied Conformity Assessment Modules and the Certificates issued as outcomes of the conformity assessment performed. The Certificates must provide the number of the certificate and where relevant also the revision number of a certificate."@en;
    dcterms:issued "2026-10-30";
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    dcterms:title "The Compliance module of an EU Digital Product Passport Core Ontology (EU DPP CO) proposed by the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "comp";
    rdfs:comment "Note1: \n\nCE-marking is applicable, if a product fulfills all requirements of product-specific Union Harmonization Legislation which need to be applied for the product. The EU-DoC must provide information for all Union Harmonisation Legislation that is applied for the product. Thus, no explicit identification of Union Harmonisation Legislation relevant for CE marking is required, as this is an intrinsic property.\n\nNote 2:\n\nAnnex V of the ESPR mentions technical documentation in addition to conformity certificates as possible data elements to include in the DPP for “compliance documentation and information required under this Regulation or other Union law applicable to the product”. These could be included as Documents in the product ontology and in an upcoming version of the compliance module references will be added."@en, "The Compliance module of an EU DPP core ontology proposed by the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    rdfs:label "EU DPP CO COMP"@en;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0".
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/CON> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "\n        Maigre, R., Robal, T., Haav, H.M., 2026. Modular ontology design approach for an ESPR compliant digital product passport core ontology,in: Joint Proceedings of Baltic DB&IS Conference Forum and Doctoral Consortium 2026 co-located with 17th International Baltic Conference on Digital Business and Intelligent Systems (Baltic DB&IS 2026), CEUR-WS.org, Tartu, Estonia. pp. 115–126. URL: https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-4211/paper11.pdf. \n        "@en;
    dcterms:contributor "Daniel Hutzschenreuter"@en, "Elio Hbeich"@en, "Fatima Danash"@en, "Marc-Andree Wolf"@en;
    dcterms:created "2025-02-27"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:creator "Riina Maigre"@en, "Tarmo Robal"@en;
    dcterms:description "Connector (Bridge) module that only defines object properties between modules. The connector contains only object properties that have domain and range specified in different modules. \n\n--\nTHIS DOCUMENT IS PROVIDED WITH NO WARRANTIES WHATSOEVER. \nAll liability for any damages arising from use or misuse of this vocabulary is with the user."@en;
    dcterms:issued "2026-10-30"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    dcterms:title "The Connector module of the EU regulatory compliant Digital Product Passport Core Ontology (EU DPP CO) proposed by the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "con";
    rdfs:comment "The CON module of the EU DPP core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    rdfs:label "EU DPP CORE CON"@en;
    owl:versionInfo "2.5.0".
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/EVENT> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15270342>;
    dcterms:contributor "Theodor Chirvasuta"@en, "Riina Maigre"@en, "Tarmo Robal"@en;
    dcterms:created "2026-03-06"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:creator "Elio Hbeich"@en;
    dcterms:description "Provides classes and properties for representing ESPR-level product and DPP events, and links product-facing events to selected GS1 EPCIS and CBV technical representation terms. Cross-module EU DPP Core Ontology relations are intended to be managed in the Connector/mapping layer."@en;
    dcterms:issued "2026-09-23"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    dcterms:title "EU DPP Core Ontology Event Module"@en;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "evt";
    rdfs:comment "Event module of the EU DPP Core Ontology. It defines ESPR-level product and DPP event concepts. Selected GS1 EPCIS and CBV terms are referenced in this file for technical event representation only; this does not imply a global owl:imports of EPCIS/CBV nor logical subclassing between GS1 Web Vocabulary concepts and EU DPP Core Ontology classes. Cross-module EU DPP Core Ontology relations are intended to be managed in the Connector/mapping layer."@en;
    rdfs:label "Event module"@en;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0";
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://w3id.org/eudpp#".
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/IDENT> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:contributor "Elio Hbeich"@en, "Riina Maigre"@en;
    dcterms:created "2026-04-13"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:creator "Tarmo Robal"@en;
    dcterms:description "MODULE: IDENT\nIdentifier module of the EU DPP core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project.\n\nThe Identifier module proposes an universal approach for identifiers used in the EU DPP CO delivered by the CIRPASS-2 European Project.  \nThe module describes identifiers used for the project through aspects and scheme references, if appropriate, granularity is added.\n---\n\nDESIGN RESTRICTION: Specific modules of the EU DPP CO need to use the Connector to establish a link to the Identifiers module. The link needs to be establsihed to a subclass of aIdentifier class, e.g., Product hasUniqueProductIdentifier ProductIdentifier.\n---\n\nDEPENDENCIES: This module may have dependencies to all  EU DPP Core Ontology (CO) modules that use different types of identifiers, including: CON, P_DPP, SOC, ACTOR, ...  \n---\n\n---\nNote on the license: This ontology is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). In case of dispute over CC BY 4.0 applicability, or in case considering the ontology as a software or part of it, this ontology is to be considered licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.\n---\n\nTHIS DOCUMENT IS PROVIDED WITH NO WARRANTIES WHATSOEVER. \nAll liability for any damages arising from use or misuse of this vocabulary is with the user."@en;
    dcterms:issued "2026-10-30"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    dcterms:title "The Identifier (IDENT) module of the EU DPP core ontology proposed by the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "ident";
    rdfs:comment "The Identifier module (IDENT) of the EU DPP core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    rdfs:label "EU DPP IDENT"@en;
    owl:versionInfo "1.3.0".
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-5";
    dcterms:creator "Fatima Danash"@en, "Marc-Andree Wolf"@en;
    dcterms:description "LCA (Life Cycle Assessment) module of an EU DPP (Digital Product Passport) core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project.\n\nSCOPE\nThis module covers the environmental-performance metadata that a DPP is required to carry under ESPR. It supports both (a) general LCA studies of any product, expressed via eudpp:LCAStudy, and (b) Environmental Product Declarations (EPDs) conforming to EN 15804+A2 with EF 3.1 characterisation, expressed via eudpp:EPDStudy (a subclass of LCAStudy). The controlled vocabulary of named individuals (impact indicators, inventory indicators, lifecycle modules, characterisation methods) follows EN 15804+A2 and EF 3.1. The module aligns structurally with the ILCD+EPD v1.3 data format (https://indatawg.github.io/ILCD-EPD-Data-Format/) and extends it with richer OWL semantics.It also relates to LCAnet/IA module (https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#).\n\nDEPENDENCIES\nThis module has dependencies to the following EU DPP Core Ontology (CO) modules: ACTOR and P_DPP via CON."@en;
    dcterms:issued "2026-10-30"@en;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    dcterms:title "LCA module of the CIRPASS-2 EU DPP Core Ontology"@en;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "eudpp";
    rdfs:comment "The LCA module of the EU DPP core ontology, version 3.1"@en;
    rdfs:label "EU DPP LCA"@en;
    owl:versionInfo 3.1;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://indatawg.github.io/ILCD-EPD-Data-Format/>, <https://standards.cen.eu/dyn/www/f?p=204:110:0::::FSP_PROJECT:65243>, <https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#>;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://w3id.org/eudpp#";
    owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA/3.1>.
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/MAT> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:contributor "Riina Maigre"@en;
    dcterms:created "2026-04-10"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:creator "Tarmo Robal"@en;
    dcterms:description "MODULE: MATERIAL\nMaterial module of the  EU DPP core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project.\n\nDEPENDENCIES:  This module has dependencies to the following EU DPP Core Ontology (CO) modules: CON, P_DPP, SOC.  \n\nUnder the ESPR, products must disclose what materials they contain, where those materials come from, whether they include substances of concern, and how those materials support durability, repairability, recyclability, and circularity.\nThe main requirements regarding materials are given in ESPR Annex I. \n\n---\nNote on the license: This ontology is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). In case of dispute over CC BY 4.0 applicability, or in case considering the ontology as a software or part of it, this ontology is to be considered licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.\n---\n\nTHIS DOCUMENT IS PROVIDED WITH NO WARRANTIES WHATSOEVER. \nAll liability for any damages arising from use or misuse of this vocabulary is with the user."@en;
    dcterms:issued "2026-10-30"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    dcterms:title "The Materials (MAT) module of the EU DPP core ontology proposed by the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "mat";
    rdfs:comment "The Material module of the EU DPP core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    rdfs:label "EU DPP MAT"@en;
    owl:versionInfo "1.2.0".
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/P_DPP> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "\n        [1] Robal, T., Maigre, R., Haav, H.M., 2026. Ontology requirements for digital product passports based on the ecodesign for sustainable products regulation. Procedia Computer Science 277, 356–365. DOI:10.1016/j.procs.2026.02.077. <br/><br/>\n\n        [2] Maigre, R., Robal, T., Haav, H.M., 2026. Modular ontology design approach for an ESPR compliant digital product passport core ontology,in: Joint Proceedings of Baltic DB&IS Conference Forum and Doctoral Consortium 2026 co-located with 17th International Baltic Conference on Digital Business and Intelligent Systems (Baltic DB&IS 2026), CEUR-WS.org, Tartu, Estonia. pp. 115–126. URL: https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-4211/paper11.pdf. <br/><br/>\n\n        [3] Maigre, R., Haav, H.-M., Robal, T., Wolf, M.-A., Danash, F. (2025). Ontology Requirements Specification for an EU DPP Core Ontology Proposal (Version 1.1). CIRPASS-2 Consortium. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15270342. <br/><br/>\n        "@en, <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15270342>;
    dcterms:contributor "Theodor Chirvasuta"@en, "Riina Maigre"@en, "Tarmo Robal"@en;
    dcterms:created "2025-01-29"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:creator "Hele-Mai Haav (up until version 1.7.1 incl.), further maintained by contributors."@en;
    dcterms:description "The EU DPP core ontology proposed in CIRPASS-2 European project  is a shared formal specification of basic concepts and properties/relationships in the cross-sectorial DPP domain to facilitate knowledge sharing across sector-specific DPPs.\n\nThe proposed  EU DPP core ontology captures several modules from which the Product and DPP module plays a central role.\n\nDEPENDENCIES:  This module has dependencies to the following EU DPP Core Ontology (CO) modules: CON, ACTOR, SOC.  \n\nFor more information, see \nMaigre, R., Haav, H.-M., Robal, T., Wolf, M.-A., & Danash, F. (2025). Ontology Requirements Specification for an EU DPP Core Ontology Proposal (1.1). CIRPASS-2 Consortium. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15270342\n\n---\nNote on the license: This ontology is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). In case of dispute over CC BY 4.0 applicability, or in case considering the ontology as a software or part of it, this ontology is to be considered licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.\n---\n\n=======================\n"@en;
    dcterms:issued "2026-10-30"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    dcterms:title "The Product and DPP module of an EU regulatory compliant Digital Product Passport Core Ontology (EU DPP CO) proposed by the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "dpp";
    rdfs:comment "The Product and DPP module of an EU DPP core ontology proposed by the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    rdfs:label "EU DPP CO P_DPP"@en;
    owl:versionInfo "2.3.0".
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/SOC> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:contributor "Hele-Mai Haav"@en;
    dcterms:created "2025-02-27"@en;
    dcterms:creator "Elio Hbeich"@en, "Tarmo Robal"@en;
    dcterms:description "MODULE: SOC\nSubstances of Concern module of the  EU DPP core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project.\n\nDEPENDENCIES:  This module has dependencies to the following EU DPP Core Ontology (CO) modules: CON, P_DPP.  \n\nThe third iteration of the Substances of Concern module of the EU DPP core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project.\n\nThe information requirements laid out in ESPR Art 7(2) and Art 7(5) for products require the information requirements to make it possible to track the substances of concern, throughout the life cycle of the products concerned. These information requirements for specific product groups are specified in the delegated acts adopted pursuant to Art 4 of ESPR.\n\t\nThis module addresses only the information requirements referred and stated in the ESPR. \n=====================================\nCONTEXT: \nRegulation (EC) No 1907/2006  Art 3(1) defines Substance: means a chemical element and its compounds in the natural state or obtained by\nany manufacturing process, including any additive necessary to preserve its stability and any impurity deriving from the process used, but excluding any solvent which may be separated without affecting the stability of the substance or changing its composition; \n\n------------------------------------------------------------------- \nKnown issues:\n - hasLifeCycleStage misses range (Event).\n\n--\nTHIS DOCUMENT IS PROVIDED WITH NO WARRANTIES WHATSOEVER. \nAll liability for any damages arising from use or misuse of this vocabulary is with the user."@en;
    dcterms:issued "2026-10-30"@en;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>;
    dcterms:title "The Substance of Concern (SOC) module of the EU DPP core ontology proposed by the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    rdfs:comment "Third iteration of the Substances of Concern module of the EU DPP core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project."@en;
    rdfs:label "EU DPP SOC"@en;
    owl:versionInfo "2.3.0";
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann#preferredNamespacePrefix> "soc".
