_:n3-65 rdf:first eudpp:batch;
    rdf:rest _:n3-66.
eudpp:batch a owl:NamedIndividual, eudpp:ProductIdentifierGranularity;
    rdfs:comment "According to ESPR Art 9 (2d) the digital product passport is to be established at model, batch or item level, and the definition of such levels is given by delegated acts;\n\nThe term ‘batch’ usually refers to a subset of a specific model composed of all products produced in a specific manufacturing plant at a specific moment in time (ESPR preamble (33))."@en;
    rdfs:label "batch"@en.
_:n3-66 rdf:first eudpp:item;
    rdf:rest _:n3-67.
eudpp:item a owl:NamedIndividual, eudpp:ProductIdentifierGranularity;
    rdfs:comment "According to ESPR Art 9 (2d) the digital product passport is to be established at model, batch or item level, and the definition of such levels is given by delegated acts;\n\nThe term ‘item’ usually refers to a single unit of a model (ESPR preamble (33))."@en;
    rdfs:label "item"@en.
_:n3-67 rdf:first eudpp:model;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
eudpp:model a owl:NamedIndividual, eudpp:ProductIdentifierGranularity;
    rdfs:comment "According to ESPR Art 9 (2d) the digital product passport is to be established at model, batch or item level, and the definition of such levels is given by delegated acts;\n\nThe term ‘model’ usually refers to a version of a product of which all units share the same technical characteristics relevant for the ecodesign requirements and the same model identifier (ESPR preamble (33))."@en;
    rdfs:label "model"@en.
